---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SignatureTool from '../../components/tools/SignatureTool.tsx';
import StepStrip from '../../components/StepStrip.astro';
---
<Base title="Signature Resize to 10–20 KB Online Free | Sign Size Reducer — FormFix India" description="Resize signature to 10–20 KB online free: resize a scanned signature to between 10 KB and 20 KB as JPEG, with cropping, background whitening and contrast, in your browser.">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol class="flex gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500"><li><a class="underline" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true">/</li><li aria-current="page">Signature Resize to 10–20 KB</li></ol></nav>
<h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-4">Signature Resize to 10–20 KB</h1>
<p class="text-slate-600 mt-2 max-w-2xl">For forms that ask for a signature between 10 KB and 20 KB. The range is checked by actual bytes (10,240–20,480). No padding is added to fake the range, and this tool never verifies handwriting authenticity.</p>
<StepStrip steps={["Choose your file", "Check the real size", "Download"]} />
<div class="mt-6"><SignatureTool client:idle /></div>
<section class="mt-10 card p-5 md:p-6"><h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold">Instructions and limits</h2><p class="mt-2 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">Sign on white paper with a dark pen, scan or photograph in good light, and crop tightly around the signature. If the output is below 10 KB, you need a larger or more detailed scan — the tool will not pad the file. If it is above 20 KB, reduce the crop or let the tool lower quality and size. A 3:1 guide matches about 6 cm × 2 cm and a 2:1 guide matches about 4 cm × 2 cm; pixel ratio alone cannot prove printed centimetres, so check your own form's notice.</p><p class="mt-2">Related: <a class="underline" href="/application-checker/">Check SSC CHT 2026 signature rules (archived)</a> · <a class="underline" href="/tools/image-to-20kb/">Image to 20 KB</a></p></section>
</Base>
